      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For increasing nitrogen without significantly altering your pH, blood meal is generally the better choice compared to bone meal. Bone meal is primarily a source of phosphorus, while blood meal offers a readily available nitrogen boost. Since your pH is already well-balanced at 6.2, using blood meal should help you meet your nitrogen needs without major pH shifts.",
